WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.180
At the start of 2024,

2
00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:07.130
there were about 5.5 million
private sector businesses in the UK.

3
00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:11.720
Nearly three in four of them employed
nobody apart from their owners.

4
00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.240
Meanwhile, some firms
grow by buying others.

5
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:20.030
In 2019, two of the country's
largest supermarkets tried to merge,

6
00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:22.690
until the competition
authority blocked it.

7
00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:26.010
Why do some firms grow
by buying up other firms,

8
00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:28.290
while most firms stay small?

9
00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:32.070
In this mission, you'll trace
the directions a firm can grow:

10
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:36.840
sideways, backward, forward,
or into something unrelated.

11
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.320
Then you'll weigh what growth can cost,

12
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.470
and why some giants
choose to split in two.

13
00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:46.070
Your mission: find out
what pushes firms to grow,

14
00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:48.120
and what holds so many of them back.
